# RPI music playhead (Oct 2026)

RPI's `MusicAssistantViewModel` collects Home Assistant `state_changed` and copies `newState` (including `mediaPosition`) onto the now-playing row. Music Assistant and other players publish `media_position` on that websocket while the track plays. Use that attribute. Do not add elapsed time on top of it — that double-counts a live position.

## Wiring

- `mediaPosition()` / `mediaProgress()` (`MusicBind.kt`) read `media_position` and `media_duration` from the entity state the websocket just wrote.
- `bindMusicNowPlaying` (full music tile) and `bindMediaBar` (free-form now-playing bar) bind `pos`, `dur`, and `progress` from those values.
- `PlayerHub` debounces `homeAssistant.states`, then `conflate().collect` so `session.refresh` finishes. `collectLatest` cancelled a slow refresh (pictures, a rebuild) and dropped later documents' vars — the bar never moved even though HA had sent a new position.
- `PlayerSession.tick` still calls `SessionDocument.tickProgress` once a second and sends only the vars that changed. That is a var update, not a document rebuild — a timed `refreshEvery` on the music tile flashes home (see `session-document-rebuild-context.mdc`).

## Layout (already shipped)

`nowPlayingProgress` (`MusicPanel.kt`) is RPI's `NowPlayingTrackTime` row: elapsed left, duration right, full-width `levelBar` under. Seek still uses `media_duration * step / PROGRESS_STEPS`.
